  "appreciation": "Standing at a cliff on the Yangtze, Su Shi lets the river wash away a thousand years of heroes and then summons Zhou Yu at his most brilliant. The contrast between the young general's glory and the poet's own early white hair gives the poem its ache. It ends by accepting the dreamlike passing of life and pouring a cup to the river moon, an image that defines the Song dynasty's philosophical grandeur.",
